Paste the new GitHub App private key here and save this file as
hack/github-app-key.pem (that name is gitignored; this .example file is not —
never paste a real key into it).

Get the key at: GitHub -> Organization settings -> Developer settings ->
GitHub Apps -> the ElasticClaw app -> Private keys -> Generate a private key.
GitHub downloads a .pem in PKCS#1 form; paste it whole, including both
delimiter lines and the trailing newline.

Then run:
    hack/rotate-github-app-key.py --check-only   # validates, writes nothing
    hack/rotate-github-app-key.py                # rotates hub + workspace

Delete hack/github-app-key.pem once the rotation is done.

-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
<paste the key body here>
-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
